\description{
Read an mzLib spectral library (.msl) as one row per precursor, or with fragments one row per fragment ion, with mzLib's not-available sentinels as nulls.

The many-files form of \code{\link{library_read}}: a predicted library and the empirical one refined from
it, say. ONE bridge process reads every library, \code{threads} at a time, into ONE table, in input
order; each library's facts (counts, load mode, format version) are its row of \code{files}.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_library_batch} (an \code{mzlibr_batch}). \code{records} begins with \code{source_index}
  (1-based, into \code{paths}) and \code{source_path}, then the columns of \code{\link{library_read}}, rows grouped
  by library in input order, each library's in \code{precursor_index} order (1-based) - \strong{whatever}
  \code{threads} \strong{was}. Their units are as there: \code{precursor_mz} and \code{fragment_mz} in m/z,
  \code{charge_state} and \code{fragment_charge} a charge, \code{retention_time} in iRT or minutes per row (read
  \code{retention_time_unit}), \code{ion_mobility} in 1/K0, \code{q_value} a fraction, \code{nce} an NCE,
  \code{fragment_count} in fragment ions, \code{fragment_intensity} a relative intensity (0 to 1) and
  \code{neutral_loss} in Da. \code{file_count}, \code{read_count} and \code{failed_count} count files; \code{record_count}
  counts precursors summed over the libraries read, \code{returned_count} the precursors returned and
  \code{row_count} the rows (one per fragment ion with \code{fragments}), both 0 with \code{out}.
  \code{fragments_included} and \code{index_only_threshold} (in bytes) are as for \code{\link{library_read}}.

  \code{files} has one row per input: the facts \code{\link{library_read}} reports at its top level, under the
  same names - \code{reader}, \code{format_version}, \code{is_compressed}, \code{is_index_only}, \code{target_count},
  \code{decoy_count}, \code{proteoform_count}, \code{min_precursor_mz}, \code{max_precursor_mz} (m/z), \code{record_count}
  (precursors), \code{caveats}, \code{absent_fields} - and \code{error_kind}, \code{error_type} and \code{error_message},
  \code{NA} for a library that was read. **For a library that could not be read, the facts it could
  not establish are \code{NA}, not zero**: nothing was counted.

}
