\section{Parameters: units, ranges and defaults}{
\describe{
\item{\code{fragments}}{flag; default \code{FALSE}. One row per fragment ion instead of one per precursor: the precursor's columns repeated on each row, then the fragment's. A precursor with no fragment ions gives one row whose fragment cells are null. Given with a value is a usage error.}
\item{\code{index_only_threshold} (wire \code{--index-only-threshold})}{int; in \strong{bytes}; default \code{1073741824}; range \code{>= 0}. Passed to MslFileTypeHandler.Open: a library this size or larger opens index-only (precursors in memory, fragment blocks read from disk on demand), a smaller one is loaded whole. Absent means mzLib's own default, MslFileTypeHandler.DefaultIndexOnlyThresholdBytes, 1073741824 bytes (1 GiB) at the pin; the bridge sends no value of its own. 0 opens every library index-only. The rows are the same in both modes; only memory and speed differ.}
\item{\code{paths} (wire \code{--paths-stdin})}{flag; default absent. Read MANY libraries: newline-delimited paths on stdin (blank lines ignored; a repeated path is a usage error). Exclusive with path; offset and limit are refused with it.}
\item{\code{threads}}{int; in \strong{files}; default \code{1}; range \code{>= 1, or -1 for one per core}. Libraries read at once. The output is byte-identical at any value (libraries are emitted in input order); 1 is the default because a library loaded whole is held in memory while its rows are written.}
\item{\code{on_error} (wire \code{--on-error})}{string; default \code{fail}; range \code{fail | skip}. fail: the first unreadable library stops the batch with its usage or correctness error, the message starting 'Input <i> (<path>)'. skip: the failure goes in that input's files[i].error and the rest are read. skip with a single path is a usage error.}
\item{\code{out}}{path; default absent; range \code{.tsv only, any case (PYB-1)}. Write the long table here, one library at a time in input order. A batch that stops on an error deletes its partial table. Must differ from every input. Must end in .tsv, any case (PYB-1); any other extension, or none, is a usage error before any input is read, and no extension is appended.}
}
}
